WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:03.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:05.667
-Does anybody know how small
this desk is?

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.300
-This is a normal size.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.534
-This is like a children-sized
desk, Jimmy.

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:11.400
-It's a normal-sized desk.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.534
Here we go.

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:16.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:17.901
Ahh.

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:19.267
How many times have you
been on our show?

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:20.834
-I think around eight.

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:22.334
-Is that correct?
-Yeah. A lot of times.

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:23.767
-Eight. So you're family here.

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:25.667
You're welcome here, but we have
it all set up for you.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:27.868
You have identical --
-You got enough Sharpies?

00:00:27.868 --> 00:00:29.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.334
-We have a lot of Sharpies
which -- I don't even know why.

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:32.634
We never even really use them.
-Yeah, you don't use them.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:34.767
-But you have props.
You have things over the side.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:36.267
-Guys, Jimmy's got some
weird stuff back here.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:37.767
-Does it feel like a small desk?

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:39.100
-You don't want to know
what's back here.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.234
-Do you feel --
It's not that small. Look.

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:42.467
We're both kind of fitting.
-Dude, this is weird.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.734
-I know. You're getting cut off.
-Yeah. My knee.

00:00:44.734 --> 00:00:47.000
This is exciting.
I'm excited for this.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.467
Alright. Here we go.
Let's do this.

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:49.300
Do you want to do this together?

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.934
-Yeah.
-Ready?

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:52.367
-We have a great show tonight.

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:55.033
As I said earlier,
Jesse Tyler Ferguson is here.

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:57.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
Shawn Mendes is here.

00:00:57.467 --> 00:01:00.467
I love that guy.

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:02.033
His new single --

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:03.133
-Oh.
-Yeah, you got to do this.

00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:05.000
-His new single,
"When You're Gone" --

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.734
-It's out right now.

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:09.534
-"When You're Gone"
is out right now.

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:11.968
-He'll be performing it here
later in the show.

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:13.534
We're gonna talk
and maybe compete

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.567
in a game of skill
involving eggs.

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:16.767
It's gonna be fun.

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:17.801
-I'm glad you're here.
-I'm glad to be here.

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:19.567
-Yeah, there you go,
Shawn Mendes.

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:24.601
I love this. Alright, good.

00:01:24.601 --> 00:01:26.667
Today is Friday, and that's
usually when I catch up

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:28.834
with some personal stuff.
-You mean like check your inbox,

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:30.901
return some e-mails, of course,
send out --

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:33.367
-Thank-you notes.
Yeah, thank-you notes.

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:36.434
I was running a bit behind,
so I thought if you guys

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:37.434
wouldn't mind,
I'd like to write out

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:38.834
my weekly thank-you notes
right now.

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:40.367
Is that cool with you guys?
-Is it cool if I write some too?

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:42.634
-Yeah, you can write some.
-Yeah, I'd love to.

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:45.000
Do I have my -- Oh, yeah, okay,
here we go.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.033
-You got your thank-you notes?
-Yeah, I got them right here.

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:49.567
-Okay. You have your pen?
-I got my pen.

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:52.501
-Okay.

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:55.901
James, can we get some thank-you
note writing music, please?

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:57.067
♪♪

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:58.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.601 --> 00:02:00.467
Don't even try to not smile.

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:02.334
[ Laughter ]
Oh, my gosh.

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:04.033
-Look at that face.
-Yeah, look at that face.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:06.133
Come on. Look at that face.

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:08.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:10.234
That's a good-looking dude.
-That's a beautiful man.

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:12.501
-Alright, here we go.

00:02:12.501 --> 00:02:13.868
♪♪

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:17.367
Thank you, NFL Draft,
for being in Las Vegas

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.934
because if there's one place
you want to hand a 22-year-old

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:21.901
$50 million, it's Las Vegas.

00:02:21.901 --> 00:02:26.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
Ooh, yeah.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.334
♪♪
-Thank you, "Top Gun: Maverick,"

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:31.467
for being the movie version
of a chest bump.

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:35.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:39.167
[ Laughter ]
That's very nice.

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:40.334
♪♪

00:02:40.334 --> 00:02:43.334
-Thank you, Dr. Fauci,
for saying the U.S.

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:45.400
is out of the pandemic phase.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.968
Though I'll believe it
when you book a Carnival cruise.

00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:54.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:54.434 --> 00:02:56.267
-Thank you, Spotify logo,

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:59.667
for looking like three worms
decided to spoon each other.

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:05.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.734
-That was a good one.
I liked that one.

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:07.767
-You like that one?
-Yeah, that was --

00:03:07.767 --> 00:03:09.200
-They gave you
all the good ones.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.634
Making me look bad
on my first time.

00:03:10.634 --> 00:03:12.467
-No, no, that was a great one.
I think you should have done

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:14.667
this one, but I like this one.
Ready?

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.167
♪♪

00:03:16.167 --> 00:03:19.467
Thank you, 7-Eleven's new
breakfast taquitos.

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:22.667
So if you didn't think those
taquitos were appetizing before,

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:24.200
now they're filled with eggs.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:35.067
Wow, you're coming --
That's almost like a sidearm.

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:38.868
-Wow.
-Wow.

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:40.334
♪♪

00:03:40.334 --> 00:03:42.200
-Thank you, windshield wipers,

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.801
for letting my car dance to
"Hip Hop Hooray."

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:46.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:50.968
♪♪

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:56.000
-♪ Hey, ho, hey, ho ♪

00:03:59.901 --> 00:04:01.300
-Oh, yeah, you unbutton.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.567
-I didn't know about
the unbutton when you sit down.

00:04:03.567 --> 00:04:06.167
-So I just kind of open up.
-Ah, this feels a lot better.

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:07.968
-Now it's like, wow, now we can
breathe a little bit

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:09.634
and hang out, come on.
-Yeah, this is great.

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:11.367
-Dude, this is perfect.
-Yeah. I like this.

00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:13.334
I could get used to this.
-I love this.

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:15.267
We should do this every --
-How you guys doing out there?

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:16.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:19.067
We could do this every night.
I love this.

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:21.801
-You need a bigger desk.

00:04:21.801 --> 00:04:24.400
-Alright. Ready?
-Okay, here we go.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:27.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:31.968
Thank you, water, for always
being the perfect duet partner.

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:34.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:36.467
-I agree.

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:38.968
No, you and water
are perfect together.

00:04:38.968 --> 00:04:40.767
-You look good with water too.

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:43.334
-No. Isn't it odd it always
rains whenever you perform?

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:45.300
-Rains, yeah.
-Yeah, indoors.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.901
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:49.133
-It's really unbelievable.
-My sleeves are never on either.

00:04:49.133 --> 00:04:51.300
-Yeah, no, exactly right.
Okay. Here we go.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.467
We'll do this one together.
-Alright, okay.

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:54.000
Yeah, yeah.
Let's see what we got. Oh.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.367
-Ready?
-Yeah.

00:04:56.367 --> 00:04:57.601
♪♪

00:04:57.601 --> 00:04:59.734
-Thank you, having a co-host,

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:03.300
for making tonight
double the fun...

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.601
-And half the work.

00:05:04.601 --> 00:05:05.601
-There you have it, everybody.

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:06.801
Those are my thank-you notes.

